  q(MW,'Since HPV vaccination began, which change has been reported among young women in the U.S.?','Fewer cervical precancers',['More HPV infections','More cervical cancer','No change in HPV types'],'D','Infections with the vaccine HPV types have dropped greatly among teen girls and young women.',MMWR),
  q(MW,'Which schedule gives the best protection against chickenpox outbreaks in schools?','Two doses of varicella vaccine',['One dose of MMR','Antibiotics after exposure','A single dose given at age 18'],'A','Outbreaks continued with one dose, so a second dose was added in 2006.',MMWR),
  q(MW,'A county of 250,000 people reports 500 cases of a disease in one year. What is the rate per 100,000?','200 per 100,000',['20 per 100,000','50 per 100,000','500 per 100,000'],'B','500 ÷ 250,000 × 100,000 = 200 cases per 100,000 population, which allows comparison across counties.',MMWR),
  q(MW,'A disease rate rises from 4 to 6 per 100,000. What is the percent increase?','50%',['2%','33%','150%'],'C','The rate went up by 2, and 2 ÷ 4 = 0.5, a 50% increase over the starting rate.',MMWR),
  q(MW,'How do U.S. wildlife programs try to stop the spread of raccoon rabies?','By dropping oral rabies vaccine baits',['By vaccinating all people','By using insecticide sprays','By giving antibiotics to raccoons'],'D','Animals eat the baits and become immune, creating barriers to the westward spread of rabies.',MMWR),
  q(MW,'Human plague cases in the U.S. occur mostly in the rural Southwest and are spread mainly by:','Fleas from infected rodents',['Mosquito bites','Contaminated water','Ticks found on deer'],'A','Pet cats and dogs can also bring infected fleas into homes, and plague is treated with antibiotics.',MMWR),
  q(MW,'Which disease, sometimes called “rabbit fever,” can spread from rabbits, ticks and deer flies?','Tularemia',['Brucellosis','Leptospirosis','Q fever from goats'],'B','Tularemia is also a potential bioterrorism agent because it can spread through the air.',MMWR),
  q(MW,'Brucellosis cases in the U.S. are most often linked to which exposure?','Unpasteurized dairy products',['Swimming pools','Undercooked chicken','Raw shellfish from warm waters'],'C','Many cases come from soft cheeses made with raw milk, often brought from other countries.',MMWR),
  q(MW,'After floods, people wading in water contaminated with animal urine may develop which infection?','Leptospirosis',['Lyme disease','Botulism','Hepatitis B'],'D','Leptospira bacteria can enter through cuts in the skin or the eyes.',MMWR),
  q(MW,'In 2001, anthrax spores were spread on purpose through which route?','Letters sent through the mail',['Contaminated beef','Drinking water','Mosquito bites in a rural town'],'A','The attacks killed five people and led to major changes in U.S. biodefense preparedness.',MMWR),
  q(MW,'About how effective are two doses of MMR vaccine at preventing measles?','About 97%',['About 50%','About 75%','100%'],'B','One dose is about 93% effective, so a second dose protects most of those who did not respond.',MMWR),
  q(MW,'Xylazine, increasingly found in illicit fentanyl, is a concern because it:','Is not reversed by naloxone',['Is a legal pain medicine for people','Has no harmful effects','Prevents overdoses'],'C','Naloxone should still be given because fentanyl is usually also present.',MMWR),
  q(MW,'During wildfires, which air pollutant from smoke poses the greatest health risk?','Fine particulate matter (PM2.5)',['Ground-level ozone','Radon gas from soil','Carbon dioxide (CO2)'],'D','Fine particles reach deep into the lungs and can worsen asthma and heart disease.',MMWR),
  q(MW,'Chronic wasting disease in deer and elk is caused by which type of agent?','A prion',['A bacterium','A virus','A parasitic worm'],'A','No human cases have been confirmed, but hunters are advised to test meat in affected areas.',MMWR),
  q(MW,'Which mosquito species is the main vector of dengue, Zika and chikungunya?','Aedes aegypti',['Culex pipiens','Anopheles gambiae','Psorophora ciliata'],'B','Aedes aegypti bites during the day and breeds in small containers of water near homes.',MMWR),
  q(MW,'In 2023, locally acquired malaria cases were reported in Florida and Texas. How are most U.S. malaria cases acquired?','During travel abroad',['From blood transfusions','From local mosquitoes every year','From person-to-person contact'],'C','Local cases were the first in 20 years, but nearly all U.S. cases are in returning travelers.',MMWR),
  q(MW,'Because of rising resistance, which treatment does the CDC recommend for uncomplicated gonorrhea?','A single shot of ceftriaxone',['Oral penicillin','Oral ciprofloxacin','No treatment'],'D','Gonorrhea has become resistant to many antibiotics, so cephalosporins are among the last options.',MMWR),
  q(MW,'Which product, recommended starting in 2023, protects infants from severe RSV with a single injection?','Nirsevimab, a monoclonal antibody',['An antibiotic','A live RSV vaccine for newborns','An antiviral pill'],'A','Infants are also protected if their mother received an RSV vaccine late in pregnancy.',MMWR),
  q(MW,'In 2024, H5N1 avian influenza spread in the U.S. among which animals for the first time?','Dairy cattle',['Pet dogs','Honeybees','Farmed fish'],'B','Human cases were mostly mild and occurred among farm workers in contact with sick animals.',MMWR),
  q(MW,'In 2024, U.S. travelers returning from Cuba were diagnosed with Oropouche virus. How does it spread?','Mainly through bites of small midges',['Through contaminated food','Through the air','Through rodent droppings'],'C','Oropouche can also pass from a pregnant person to the fetus, so pregnant travelers were warned.',MMWR),
  q(MW,'In 2023, high blood lead levels in young children were traced to which product?','Cinnamon applesauce pouches',['Infant formula','Drinking water fountains','Crayons'],'D','The cinnamon came from a supplier abroad and contained very high levels of lead.',MMWR),
  q(MW,'An epidemic curve is a histogram. What does each bar usually represent?','The number of cases with onset during a time interval',['One person','The death rate in the community that week','The number of laboratory tests performed during each week'],'A','The time interval chosen is often about one-quarter to one-third of the average incubation period.',MMWR),
  q(MW,'What does the sensitivity of a surveillance system describe?','The share of true cases it detects',['How quickly it reports data','How cheap it is','How many groups use its reports'],'B','A system with low sensitivity misses cases but can still show trends if reporting stays steady.',MMWR)
